### Log in first (as the seeded teacher) and copy the token from the response into
### the Authorization header below - don't hardcode a real token here, it becomes
### stale the moment the secret rotates or the token expires (and shouldn't be committed)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "teacher@example.com",
  "password": "temp123"
}

###

POST http://localhost:8080/teacher/register
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN_RESPONSE_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student1@example.com",
  "password": "temp123",
  "firstName": "Avi",
  "lastName": "Cohen",
  "phone": "0501234567",
  "hourlyRate": 120,
  "educationLevel": "11th grade"
}